\title{The BCS Transform}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    How an IOP plus a commitment scheme becomes a non-interactive argument. The transform that every hash-based system in deployment is an instance of.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The construction: commit to each oracle, answer queries with openings, then [Fiat–Shamir](dhsorens-002G).}
        \li{What the commitment must provide — position binding is not obviously enough; where extractability is needed.}
        \li{How the IOP's query complexity turns into proof size, concretely.}
        \li{The security loss in the reduction, and whether it is tight.}
        \li{ArkLib's \code{OracleReduction/BCS}: what is formalised and what the statement looks like.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: Ben-Sasson, Chiesa, and Spooner, \em{Interactive Oracle Proofs}; [ArkLib](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/ArkLib).
}
